{"title":"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular grazing area is to be fenced off on three sides using part of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> meter rock wall as the fourth side.  Fence posts are to be placed every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> meters along the fence including the two posts where the fence meets the rock wall.  What is the fewest number of posts required to fence an area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa414977bf516314bc2cfefbe5c31c688401ec44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(12); draw((0,0)--(16,12)); draw((16/3,4)--(32/3,8)--(20/3,40/3)--(4/3,28/3)--cycle); draw((16/3 +.4,4+.3)--(16/3 +.1,4+.7)--(16/3-.3,4+.4)); draw((32/3 -.3,8+.4)--(32/3 -.7,8+.1)--(32/3-.4,8-.3)); draw((20/3 -.4,40/3-.3)--(20/3 -.1,40/3-.7)--(20/3+.3,40/3-.4)); draw((4/3 +.3,28/3-.4)--(4/3 +.7,28/3-.1)--(4/3+.4,28/3+.3)); label(&quot;WALL&quot;,(7,4),SE); [/asy]\" width=\"322\" height=\"268\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/679204315f29c9465a0cadf008f27e7dd598d4a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 11 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 13 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 14 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To minimize the total length of the fence, one of the longer (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m) sides of the rectangle must touch the wall.  In this case, the total length of the fence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2f810bdc191622c7fd3fbd37d640d19eb15af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 + 60 + 36 = 132$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"15\" /> m.  Since pairs of consecutive posts are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m apart, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bfd15237ac4e688943c8afd4bc9b0a079e17ea8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$132 \\div 12 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> intervals between consecutive posts, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79bc2e069660fc764ea6f5ac5f5813cb336356ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"139\" height=\"30\" /> posts are needed.  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution 1, one of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m sides must touch the wall.  The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m side not touching the wall has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f6cf77a036b192dd3a1e863f7d3df944e794468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60 \\div 12 + 1 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" /> posts.  Each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m sides has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88cd1d9828a2030263c0475ebced0cdac5e639eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 \\div 12 + 1 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" /> posts.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> posts are at intersections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m sides, there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/861e9d134cbf7c3a6df05f2eaa105a0236a26b81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 2 \\cdot 4 - 2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"183\" height=\"30\" /> posts.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME\" title=\"1986 AJHSME\">1986 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\